omx-plugins (0.20.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Makefile: presets-figures once in make test, no install-pins phony
  * packaging: every omx-clap floor is 0.34.1
  * param contract: a unit is served by the sheet's own token (dbPerOct)
  * packaging: git is a build dependency of %check
  * make test: a red part no longer hides the others
  * face: a remote-controls page of blank slots alone is not served
  * role-meanings-source: mirror the domains kept outside the major
  * no shipped pins: our plugins are qualified like any plugin
  * the old-home grep: the deb cells comment names libomx-clap-dev
  * resource hints: the words are read from omx-contract, their owner today;
    sorting row V28 waits for its design
  * units: the vendor block is omx-contract 3.21.0's eight, and dB/oct is
    served as dbperoct (clap#163)
  * packaging: every floor on a package this delivery releases is its
    delivered version
  * gen: the descriptors, params headers and LV2 ttl carry 0.20.0
    (hand-applied gen output)
  * changelog: omx-plugins 0.20.0 (spec %changelog, debian/changelog)
  * release: the version moves to 0.20.0 (Makefile VERSION, spec Version)
  * Green: the oracle rates are read as omx-dsp's ORACLE_FULL_RATES (sorting
    row V25, B2's finding)
  * Red: the oracle rates are omx-dsp's ORACLE_FULL_RATES, read from nowhere
    else (sorting row V25, B2's finding)
  * V23d out of this chain: the unit codes are read from omx-contract's sheet
    again, as on main (%4 ruling 2026-11-20)
  * Red: no file reads omx-clap's omx-param-contract; the unit codes are
    omx-contract's sheet (%4 ruling: V23d out of this chain)
  * Green: the generator keeps a stated sweep, and the omx-contract floor is
    3.21.0
